1
00:08:23,076 --> 00:08:29,076
What one loves about life are the things that fade.

2
00:16:46,153 --> 00:16:52,153
Heaven's Gate is a drama, western film directed by Michael Cimino.

3
00:25:09,230 --> 00:25:15,230
Harvard graduate James Averill serves as the sheriff of prosperous Jackson County, Wyoming, standing at
the center of a conflict between impoverished immigrants and affluent cattle farmers.

4
00:33:32,307 --> 00:33:38,307
Politically connected ranchers enlist mercenary Nathan Champion—who is also vying for the
affections of local madam Ella Watson—to combat the immigrant uprising.

5
00:41:55,384 --> 00:42:01,384
As tensions escalate, both Averill and Champion
start to question their decisions.

6
00:50:18,461 --> 00:50:24,461
James Averill, played by Kris Kristofferson.

7
00:58:41,538 --> 00:58:47,538
Nathan D. Champion, played by Christopher Walken.

8
01:07:04,615 --> 01:07:10,615
Billy Irvine, played by John Hurt.

9
01:15:27,692 --> 01:15:33,692
Frank Canton, played by Sam Waterston.

10
01:23:50,769 --> 01:23:56,769
Mr. Eggleston, played by Brad Dourif.

11
01:32:13,846 --> 01:32:19,846
Ella Watson, played by Isabelle Huppert.

12
01:40:36,923 --> 01:40:42,923
Heaven's Gate is a 1980 American epic Western film written and directed by Michael Cimino, starring Kris Kristofferson, Christopher Walken, John
Hurt, Sam Waterston, Brad Dourif, Isabelle Huppert, Jeff Bridges, and Joseph Cotten, and loosely based on the Johnson County War.

13
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:06,000
It revolves around a dispute between land barons and European
immigrants of modest means in Wyoming in the 1890s.

14
01:57:23,076 --> 01:57:29,076
The film's production faced numerous setbacks, including cost overruns, significant retakes, bad press (including
allegations of animal abuse on set), and rumors about Cimino's allegedly authoritarian directorial style.

15
02:05:46,153 --> 02:05:52,153
Cimino had an expensive and ambitious vision for the film,
pushing it nearly four times over its planned budget.

16
02:14:09,230 --> 02:14:15,230
The film premiered in November 1980 and received significant critical
backlash, prompting United Artists (UA) to pull it from theaters.

17
02:22:32,307 --> 02:22:38,307
In April 1981, a truncated re-cut version was released, though it remained a financial failure,
earning only $3.5 million against its $44 million budget and was lambasted by critics.

18
02:30:55,384 --> 02:31:01,384
It was condemned as one of the worst films ever made at the time.

19
02:39:18,461 --> 02:39:24,461
According to some film historians such as Peter Biskind, the film's financial failure resulted in the demise of
director-driven film production in the American film industry, steering back toward greater studio control of films.

20
02:47:41,538 --> 02:47:47,538
The film's failure also led to Transamerica selling UA to
Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (MGM), ending their existence as an independent studio.

21
02:56:04,615 --> 02:56:10,615
In the decades since the release, however, general assessment
of Heaven's Gate has become more favorable.

22
03:04:27,692 --> 03:04:33,692
The 1981 re-edit has been characterized as "one of the greatest injustices of
cinematic history", while later re-edits have received critical acclaim.

23
03:12:50,769 --> 03:12:56,769
In 2015, BBC Culture ranked Heaven's Gate 98th on its list of
the 100 greatest American films of all time.

24
03:21:13,846 --> 03:21:19,846
The film explores themes of immigrant, showdown,
wyoming, usa, love triangle, montana.

25
03:29:36,923 --> 03:29:42,923
The tone is emotional.
